 R←Test_Open_089(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;parms;json;qdmx;threw;success;log
⍝ A "lx" function that is dyadic cannot be called at all, and that must be reported as a failure
⍝ rather than passed over.\\
⍝ `ExecUnderTrap` used to print its complaint straight to the session and then fall through to
⍝ `success←1`, so `HandleLX` was told the function had run, said nothing, and the project opened as
⍝ though all was well. A dyadic "lx" is a mistake in the package config and has to be visible.\\
⍝ Batch mode makes it deterministic: `HandleLX` then executes "lx" without asking, and throws.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetFolderInTempDir⊃⎕SI
 #.⎕SHADOW'TEMP' ⋄ 'TEMP'#.⎕NS''
 tempDir ⎕NCOPY⍠('Wildcard' 1)⊣##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/LxProject/*'

⍝ `⎕NPUT`'s left argument is (content [encoding] [nl]), so the lines must be enclosed
 (⊂' r←a DyadicOnPurpose b' ' r←a+b')⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/APLSource/DateAndTime/DyadicOnPurpose.aplf')1
 json←⊃⎕NGET tempDir,'/apl-package.json'
 json←'lx: "Init"'⎕R'lx: "DyadicOnPurpose"'⊢json
 (⊂json)⎕NPUT(tempDir,'/apl-package.json')1

 parms←##.Cider.CreateOpenParms ⍬
 parms.folder←tempDir
 parms.parent←'#.TEMP'
 parms.batch←1
 parms.ignoreUserExec←1

 threw←0
 :Trap 0
     (success log)←##.Cider.OpenProject parms
 :Else
     threw←1
     qdmx←⎕DMX
 :EndTrap
 →T.GoToTidyUp~threw

 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'Executing "lx"'⍷qdmx.EM
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'dyadic'⍷qdmx.EM
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'DyadicOnPurpose'⍷qdmx.EM

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 {}##.Cider.CloseProject'#.TEMP.DateAndTime'
 {}⎕SE.Link.Break'#.TEMP.DateAndTime'
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir,'/..'
⍝Done
